# Derived by hand, never run here (prismc refuses the program): Semantics ch. 7, "A dynamic is a sample and an update event" (a hold stepped by `!outcome` at n fires `!Updated $state` at n with the same value), so reading the parameter `!outcome` in the supplier's arm gives what attempt 11 gets from `let !stepped = !Updated $state`; the ticks below are the transcript prismc at 10ca993 gave for attempt 11 (sem-ch09-hosting-per-role-named-update), whose test is the same.
